[FEN "2r1kb1r/pp4pp/1n3p2/4pb2/1n6/1BP2PB1/PP1N2PP/2KRN2R b k - 0 1"]

 { The success of your calculation heavily depends on the tactical motifs you spot. In the Burger Technique chapter, we have learnt a few general ones (e.g., unprotected pieces, trappable pieces, critical squares) . However, you are not limited to these motifs. With PIE, you can acquire new motifs that will influence your calculation. For example, in this position, our strong light-squared Bishop pointing at White’s King combined with our Rook’s pressure on c3 counts as tactical motifs because they resemble the preconditions of Boden’s mate. Given these clues, the goal is to land our dark-squared Bishop on a3, but our b4 Knight is currently in the way. Therefore, we must look for a move that efficiently gets rid of our Knight, and what better way than to do so with check? } 1... { -KEY- } Nxa2+ 2. Bxa2 Rxc3+ 3. bxc3 ( 3. Nc2 Rxc2 4. Kb1 Rxd2 ) 
Ba3# { For an additional example with explanations, I refer you to this page } 
