 { White to play and win. } 1. { -KEY- } Qc2 Bd7 { Saving the Bishop } 2. Bb5 { Threatening Qc8# and Bb4 to trap the Black Queen } Na6 { Covering c8 and b4 } 3. Bxd7+ Kxd7 4. Rxb7+ Ke8 5. Qc6+ Kd8 6. Qd7# { Mate. If you got it wrong, ask yourself the key question, “What could you have done to find all these moves?”. If you got it right, how could you have found the moves more efficiently? In either case, I’d like you to write down your response before moving to the next page or watching the video. If you are clueless, do not fret. With the benefit of having the correct moves now revealed, try to execute the Burger Technique on the initial position. } 
